1
00:00:09,350 --> 00:00:10,570
I'm asking you one more time.

2
00:00:11,480 --> 00:00:12,380
Where's the stuff?

3
00:00:12,430 --> 00:00:13,570
I'm telling you, you're crazy!

4
00:00:13,590 --> 00:00:15,250
Where'd you get this junk?

5
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:17,500
What are you trying to say?

6
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:18,850
This isn't our product!

7
00:00:18,870 --> 00:00:19,620
Nonsense!

8
00:00:19,640 --> 00:00:20,740
Then what is this?

9
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:47,220
Our product has always been top quality.

10
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:50,010
Lots of smoke, barely any residue.

11
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:53,730
This isn't ours.

12
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:00,650
What... What's different about it?

13
00:01:00,670 --> 00:01:01,690
How can you tell?

14
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:07,330
Boss, that's impossible.

15
00:01:07,510 --> 00:01:08,740
I put it in there myself.

16
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:10,260
And I took it out with my own hands.

17
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:12,020
There's no way!

18
00:01:14,960 --> 00:01:15,890
Where's the fuse box?

19
00:01:16,070 --> 00:01:17,290
Could the fuse have blown?

20
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:18,740
Hang on.

21
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:19,680
I'll check upstairs.

22
00:01:54,580 --> 00:01:55,900
It's Curly, it must be him, Boss.

23
00:01:56,590 --> 00:01:58,020
I... I considered that possibility before.

24
00:01:58,040 --> 00:01:59,930
But I didn't think he could handle a shipment this big.

25
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:01,820
Boss, give me five days.

26
00:02:02,150 --> 00:02:04,050
Or I'll... I'll get the stuff back.

27
00:02:04,070 --> 00:02:04,540
You...

28
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:22,500
Three days.

29
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,260
I want an answer in three days.

30
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:29,130
Guo, take him out.

31
00:04:04,860 --> 00:04:06,300
[The Story Untold]

32
00:04:06,300 --> 00:04:08,940
[Based on Twentine's novel "The Story Untold" on jjwxc.net]

33
00:04:09,260 --> 00:04:12,140
[Episode 3]

34
00:04:30,610 --> 00:04:32,880
How did you know the stuff was fake?

35
00:04:39,270 --> 00:04:40,310
The wrapping paper is different.

36
00:04:40,830 --> 00:04:43,290
I went with Liu Wei to inspect this shipment.

37
00:04:43,310 --> 00:04:44,810
It's from the Eight-Faced Buddha in Zhalan.

38
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:46,780
He's always used Zhalan paper.

39
00:04:47,730 --> 00:04:48,850
It's darker than this.

40
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:08,190
How many years has it been since Mingkun?

41
00:05:10,950 --> 00:05:11,750
Seven years.

42
00:05:15,340 --> 00:05:16,870
Seven years have flown by.

43
00:05:19,310 --> 00:05:21,810
You helped me, then left halfway through.

44
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:23,380
Now you're back again.

45
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:26,900
It must be fate.

46
00:05:28,150 --> 00:05:30,420
A lot of people have been after our supply lately.

47
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:32,330
When they can't get to our suppliers,

48
00:05:32,710 --> 00:05:34,620
they go after the people around us.

49
00:05:36,470 --> 00:05:38,740
So you need to be extra careful.

50
00:05:39,590 --> 00:05:40,810
It's not just the police.

51
00:05:42,270 --> 00:05:43,060
Our rivals,

52
00:05:43,910 --> 00:05:45,180
and even our own people.

53
00:05:46,130 --> 00:05:46,860
Understood?

54
00:06:22,030 --> 00:06:22,890
What's this?

55
00:06:23,590 --> 00:06:25,250
Is it a sample brought in from overseas?

56
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:26,330
It's all in English.

57
00:06:26,470 --> 00:06:27,940
Yeah, a new sample.

58
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:29,620
Here, try one.

59
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:33,660
Blood pressure medication.

60
00:06:34,030 --> 00:06:34,860
One pill a day.

61
00:06:34,880 --> 00:06:35,890
Take it with food.

62
00:06:36,830 --> 00:06:38,300
Stop thinking about your cases all the time.

63
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:39,980
Can't you take better care of yourself?

64
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:40,890
Kid.

65
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:44,740
Chen Meilu?

66
00:06:46,320 --> 00:06:47,540
Bai Ji wants me to go see her.

67
00:06:48,760 --> 00:06:50,010
I need you to meet someone for me.

68
00:06:52,790 --> 00:06:54,010
Chen Meilu and her brother

69
00:06:54,030 --> 00:06:55,450
control the drug distribution network

70
00:06:55,470 --> 00:06:56,740
along the southern coast.

71
00:06:57,320 --> 00:06:59,620
They used to deal exclusively with Yan Nanshan.

72
00:07:00,230 --> 00:07:03,300
Right. Nanhu has been her territory for years.

73
00:07:04,640 --> 00:07:06,740
Bai Ji used to bring drugs in from across the border

74
00:07:07,150 --> 00:07:08,660
and supply them to Yan Nanshan for distribution.

75
00:07:09,270 --> 00:07:10,210
So my guess is

76
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:12,450
Bai Ji came back to Nanhu

77
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:14,570
to get rid of Yan Nanshan

78
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:16,740
and deal directly with Chen Meilu.

79
00:07:20,230 --> 00:07:22,180
Bringing drugs across the border carries the greatest risk.

80
00:07:22,910 --> 00:07:25,010
Why would anyone want to share the profits?

81
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:26,860
That makes sense.

82
00:07:28,350 --> 00:07:29,210
But there's one more thing.

83
00:07:30,320 --> 00:07:32,300
With the stock Bai Ji currently has,

84
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:37,300
he barely has enough to prove his worth.

85
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:39,450
If he wants to cut Yan Nanshan out,

86
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:41,540
I doubt that's enough.

87
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:44,250
I'll keep an eye on things.

88
00:07:45,150 --> 00:07:46,860
When are you meeting Chen Meilu?

89
00:07:48,270 --> 00:07:50,180
I don't know. He told me to wait.

90
00:07:50,710 --> 00:07:51,810
That's how he operates.

91
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:54,660
He never tells you what he's decided

92
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,740
until the very last minute.

93
00:07:57,740 --> 00:07:59,300
He doesn't trust anyone.

94
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:03,420
Ever since Mingkun's gang was taken down,

95
00:08:03,760 --> 00:08:06,060
Bai Ji has been hiding overseas.

96
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:08,570
He's gone to great lengths to establish himself in Nanhu.

97
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:10,690
I think he still has something up his sleeve.

98
00:08:11,080 --> 00:08:11,620
Here's what we'll do.

99
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:13,770
Since they want you to meet Chen Meilu,

100
00:08:13,790 --> 00:08:14,250
I think we should

101
00:08:14,270 --> 00:08:16,060
use this opportunity to follow the trail.

102
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:20,300
We'll take down the entire drug network

103
00:08:20,440 --> 00:08:21,300
in Nanhu.

104
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:24,420
It's almost over.

105
00:08:24,910 --> 00:08:25,620
Don't worry.

106
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,100
Whether it'll ever end,

107
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:31,060
you know better than anyone.

108
00:08:32,160 --> 00:08:34,540
First, we took down Mingkun's organization.

109
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:36,140
Then came Tiger,

110
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:37,660
followed by Yan Nanshan.

111
00:08:38,160 --> 00:08:39,610
Now Bai Ji has turned up.

112
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:41,450
Who knows who'll appear next?

113
00:08:42,630 --> 00:08:43,660
Over?

114
00:08:45,320 --> 00:08:46,210
I know.

115
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:50,940
You've suffered a lot over the years.

116
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:54,850
Out of 365 days in a year,

117
00:08:55,350 --> 00:08:57,140
you spend 364 of them waiting.

118
00:09:03,040 --> 00:09:04,690
But that day will come.

119
00:09:06,680 --> 00:09:07,570
Chen Mingsheng.

120
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:12,090
That's the day we've been waiting for.

121
00:09:16,870 --> 00:09:18,060
Chen Mingsheng.

122
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:21,810
I haven't heard this name in so long.

123
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:24,300
It actually feels a little strange.

124
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:52,080
Doctor, the patient in bed five is awake.

125
00:09:54,830 --> 00:09:56,060
She suffered a minor blow to the head.

126
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:57,610
She lost consciousness from smoke inhalation.

127
00:09:57,960 --> 00:09:58,690
If you're concerned,

128
00:09:58,710 --> 00:09:59,490
you can order a scan

129
00:09:59,510 --> 00:10:00,540
to rule out pulmonary edema.

130
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:02,090
Does she have any family?

131
00:10:08,160 --> 00:10:08,940
Excuse me.

132
00:10:09,680 --> 00:10:10,660
Was there someone else

133
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:12,020
brought here with me?

134
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:14,380
There was a man in bed four.

135
00:10:14,830 --> 00:10:16,900
You two came in together last night.

136
00:10:17,080 --> 00:10:18,610
But he left early this morning.

137
00:10:19,280 --> 00:10:20,060
He left?

138
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:20,610
Yes.

139
00:10:30,260 --> 00:10:32,060
[Jiang Ming]

140
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:36,610
Sorry, the number you have dialed

141
00:10:36,630 --> 00:10:37,970
is currently unavailable.

142
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:39,450
Please try again later.

143
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:43,020
Last night, on Longshan Road in Jinxian District,

144
00:10:43,040 --> 00:10:45,140
[Fire broke out on Longshan Rd., Jinxian Dist.]
a low-rise building caught fire.

145
00:10:45,510 --> 00:10:46,900
The fire was quickly brought under control.

146
00:10:47,350 --> 00:10:49,020
The injured were taken to the hospital.

147
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:50,970
The exact cause is still under investigation.

148
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:53,210
We'd also like to remind all residents...

149
00:10:53,230 --> 00:10:53,850
Ms. Yang.

150
00:10:54,990 --> 00:10:56,180
Your friend left this here

151
00:10:56,200 --> 00:10:57,690
for us to give you before he left.

152
00:11:03,040 --> 00:11:04,180
Did he say anything?

153
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:06,900
No. Just that we had to keep it safe

154
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:07,780
and give it to you personally.

155
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:32,500
Sir.

156
00:11:33,990 --> 00:11:34,690
There's something I want to talk to you about.

157
00:11:34,710 --> 00:11:35,140
Go ahead.

158
00:11:37,920 --> 00:11:39,810
I'd like to apply for witness protection.

159
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:42,730
For whom?

160
00:11:43,490 --> 00:11:44,630
The tenant from the bar.

161
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:47,420
Yesterday, Liu Wei went to pick up the stuff

162
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:48,610
and set someone's bar on fire.

163
00:11:49,590 --> 00:11:51,730
I think he's still upset about losing the shipment.

164
00:11:52,110 --> 00:11:53,060
I'm afraid he'll retaliate.

165
00:11:57,510 --> 00:11:58,780
I checked out that tenant.

166
00:11:59,230 --> 00:12:00,020
She's clean.

167
00:12:04,680 --> 00:12:06,230
Now tell me what happened

168
00:12:06,230 --> 00:12:06,940
to your hand.

169
00:12:09,630 --> 00:12:11,730
Just a scratch. Nothing serious.

170
00:12:11,990 --> 00:12:13,300
You were protecting a witness?

171
00:12:17,230 --> 00:12:18,020
A woman?

172
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:25,900
She's a young woman who came to Nanhu alone.

173
00:12:26,050 --> 00:12:27,140
Everything was fine before.

174
00:12:27,140 --> 00:12:29,020
Now she's in serious trouble because of me.

175
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:30,690
I can't put her in danger.

176
00:12:34,310 --> 00:12:35,230
Can you do it?

177
00:12:39,920 --> 00:12:41,900
Fine. I promise.

178
00:12:42,510 --> 00:12:44,140
I'll make sure she's safe.

179
00:12:45,350 --> 00:12:46,490
But don't carry this burden alone.

180
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:50,610
And don't put yourself at risk.

181
00:12:51,330 --> 00:12:52,290
Speaking of retaliation,

182
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:55,260
shouldn't you be more careful yourself?

183
00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:57,090
You're letting your feelings cloud your judgment.

184
00:12:57,830 --> 00:12:58,730
At a time like this,

185
00:12:58,750 --> 00:13:00,180
I won't allow any complications.

186
00:13:00,870 --> 00:13:02,330
If you really want to protect her,

187
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:05,450
you need to keep your distance.

188
00:13:52,320 --> 00:13:52,940
Sorry.

189
00:13:53,440 --> 00:13:55,900
The number you have dialed is currently unavailable.

190
00:13:56,110 --> 00:13:57,330
Please try again later.

191
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:37,540
Now you decide to look for me.

192
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:39,300
You must be hungry.

193
00:14:59,120 --> 00:14:59,740
Ms. Yang.

194
00:14:59,920 --> 00:15:01,890
I'm Officer Zhou. I handled the scene yesterday.

195
00:15:03,470 --> 00:15:03,960
Hello.

196
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:05,260
We were just on patrol

197
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:07,160
when we noticed a light on inside.

198
00:15:07,160 --> 00:15:07,940
So we came to check.

199
00:15:09,110 --> 00:15:10,570
I'm packing my things.

200
00:15:10,750 --> 00:15:11,330
Here's the situation.

201
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:13,210
Based on what we found at the scene,

202
00:15:13,230 --> 00:15:14,520
we still can't completely rule out

203
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:15,920
the possibility of arson.

204
00:15:16,360 --> 00:15:17,540
The exact cause is still under investigation.

205
00:15:17,830 --> 00:15:18,640
For your own safety,

206
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:21,310
you should find somewhere else to stay temporarily.

207
00:15:21,680 --> 00:15:24,150
Okay. I'll leave once I've packed.

208
00:15:24,590 --> 00:15:26,140
All right. Stay safe.

209
00:15:26,160 --> 00:15:26,780
Thank you.

210
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:48,260
When a cat gets cranky

211
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:49,180
and stops eating,

212
00:15:49,680 --> 00:15:51,420
there's a good chance it's got a hairball stuck in its stomach.

213
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:53,450
Just give it something green.

214
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:55,300
Cats eat vegetables?

215
00:16:05,140 --> 00:16:06,900
♪I don't say much♪

216
00:16:06,940 --> 00:16:08,660
♪But there's so much going on inside♪

217
00:16:08,780 --> 00:16:12,100
♪I grow more silent as time goes by♪

218
00:16:12,260 --> 00:16:15,220
♪Hard to figure out...♪

219
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:19,300
Ming, you're amazing.

220
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:20,570
Just as you predicted.

221
00:16:20,750 --> 00:16:21,690
Liu Wei couldn't hold back any longer.

222
00:16:21,710 --> 00:16:23,420
He's taking his men to collect the shipment himself.

223
00:16:23,680 --> 00:16:24,450
When?

224
00:16:24,830 --> 00:16:26,060
Probably in the next couple of days.

225
00:16:27,040 --> 00:16:28,330
With Liu Wei getting involved,

226
00:16:28,350 --> 00:16:29,730
that woman is in for a rough time.

227
00:16:30,680 --> 00:16:31,730
That's what she gets for talking back to me.

228
00:16:33,590 --> 00:16:34,730
Someone's following me.

229
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:36,610
I know. Keep going.

230
00:16:37,590 --> 00:16:38,780
Take the stairs on your right.

231
00:16:38,900 --> 00:16:44,540
♪The more I try to escape, the deeper I fall♪

232
00:16:44,740 --> 00:16:45,780
♪Please...♪

233
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:46,450
Yang Zhao.

234
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:48,450
Yang Zhao.

235
00:16:49,510 --> 00:16:50,300
Yang Zhao!

236
00:16:50,300 --> 00:16:53,380
♪I'm too earnest, too fragile♪

237
00:16:53,580 --> 00:16:56,780
♪I may seem carefree♪

238
00:16:56,980 --> 00:17:00,340
♪But I'm hurting more than anyone♪

239
00:17:00,460 --> 00:17:03,740
♪Don't see right through me so easily♪

240
00:17:03,980 --> 00:17:07,060
♪Afraid of crowds, afraid of loneliness♪

241
00:17:07,260 --> 00:17:12,060
♪Afraid I'll fall hopelessly in love with you...♪

242
00:17:24,880 --> 00:17:26,420
If you really want to protect her,

243
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:28,760
you need to keep your distance.

244
00:17:29,460 --> 00:17:32,420
♪A tenderness I was born with♪

245
00:17:32,580 --> 00:17:35,180
♪So easily traps me♪

246
00:17:36,500 --> 00:17:39,100
♪A greeting offered out of courtesy♪

247
00:17:39,420 --> 00:17:42,820
♪Captures me in a second♪

248
00:17:43,420 --> 00:17:46,020
♪Standing at a crossroads♪

249
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:49,860
♪I don't know what to do♪

250
00:17:49,940 --> 00:17:51,420
♪My heart♪

251
00:17:51,620 --> 00:17:55,220
♪Floats in midair♪

252
00:18:19,900 --> 00:18:23,580
[Body Transfer Area]

253
00:18:40,860 --> 00:18:45,500
[In Loving Memory]

254
00:18:48,710 --> 00:18:49,490
Mei.

255
00:18:56,360 --> 00:18:57,050
Please.

256
00:18:58,600 --> 00:18:59,420
Mei.

257
00:19:00,400 --> 00:19:01,730
Long time no see.

258
00:19:03,990 --> 00:19:04,770
Jiang Ming.

259
00:19:08,570 --> 00:19:10,140
I've met many of Bai Ji's men,

260
00:19:11,270 --> 00:19:12,490
but I don't remember you.

261
00:19:13,600 --> 00:19:14,380
Where's Liu Wei?

262
00:19:15,550 --> 00:19:16,340
This time,

263
00:19:16,990 --> 00:19:18,940
Mr. Bai sent me to negotiate with you.

264
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:23,140
Have we met before?

265
00:19:23,640 --> 00:19:24,580
In Maojiang.

266
00:19:25,230 --> 00:19:26,100
Six years ago.

267
00:19:27,030 --> 00:19:29,210
It was your first trip to the border to collect a shipment.

268
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:31,320
Hmm.

269
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:45,290
That doesn't seem right.

270
00:19:48,550 --> 00:19:49,970
You're exactly my type.

271
00:19:50,550 --> 00:19:51,860
How could I not remember you?

272
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:56,530
Mei,

273
00:19:57,920 --> 00:19:59,290
important people have so much on their minds.

274
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:01,450
Our operation went very smoothly that time.

275
00:20:02,510 --> 00:20:03,490
But who would've thought

276
00:20:04,270 --> 00:20:06,690
you'd turn around and work with Yan Nanshan?

277
00:20:11,600 --> 00:20:12,940
Mr. Bai holds grudges.

278
00:20:15,470 --> 00:20:15,940
Here.

279
00:20:18,600 --> 00:20:21,180
Yan Nanshan really ran out of luck.

280
00:20:22,360 --> 00:20:24,660
The police have been watching him closely lately.

281
00:20:25,600 --> 00:20:27,010
He was at the end of his rope.

282
00:20:28,470 --> 00:20:30,100
I found a place for him.

283
00:20:30,840 --> 00:20:32,380
That should satisfy Mr. Bai.

284
00:20:43,230 --> 00:20:44,180
Take a good look.

285
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:50,140
Yan Nanshan is lying right here.

286
00:20:51,230 --> 00:20:53,290
I've already proven my sincerity.

287
00:20:54,120 --> 00:20:55,380
Go back and tell Bai Ji

288
00:20:55,680 --> 00:20:57,660
the rest is up to him.

289
00:20:58,360 --> 00:21:00,180
But let me make one thing clear.

290
00:21:00,640 --> 00:21:02,420
I'm not interested in ordinary stuff.

291
00:21:03,400 --> 00:21:04,580
He made me a promise.

292
00:21:04,600 --> 00:21:05,580
If he can't deliver,

293
00:21:06,120 --> 00:21:07,530
I won't let it slide.

294
00:21:09,600 --> 00:21:10,380
Understood.

295
00:21:13,700 --> 00:21:17,740
[Empty Furnace]

296
00:21:33,020 --> 00:21:36,300
[Yan Nanshan]

297
00:21:41,220 --> 00:21:43,900
[Yan Nanshan]

298
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:57,100
Looks like things are about to change in Nanhu.

299
00:22:02,310 --> 00:22:03,690
Mr. Bai doesn't trust me.

300
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:08,140
What's wrong?

301
00:22:11,440 --> 00:22:13,290
Mr. Bai sent me to see Chen Meilu,

302
00:22:14,680 --> 00:22:16,100
but you didn't tell me anything.

303
00:22:18,160 --> 00:22:20,250
I don't even know what kind of product

304
00:22:20,270 --> 00:22:21,450
you two are planning to trade.

305
00:22:22,960 --> 00:22:24,210
What do you take me for?

306
00:22:28,030 --> 00:22:31,050
Besides, just to sell some heroin and meth,

307
00:22:31,920 --> 00:22:34,100
Chen Meilu wouldn't have killed Yan Nanshan

308
00:22:34,120 --> 00:22:35,690
to win us over, would she?

309
00:22:49,920 --> 00:22:50,690
Take a look.

310
00:23:03,120 --> 00:23:04,420
This is something new.

311
00:23:05,400 --> 00:23:06,450
It's called the zombie drug.

312
00:23:08,030 --> 00:23:10,010
Meth and heroin

313
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:12,140
are both extremely addictive.

314
00:23:13,230 --> 00:23:14,250
But this stuff

315
00:23:14,920 --> 00:23:16,730
is more than ten times as potent.

316
00:23:17,920 --> 00:23:20,340
And it's even cheaper to produce than meth.

317
00:23:22,230 --> 00:23:23,250
More importantly,

318
00:23:24,020 --> 00:23:27,250
it's not a controlled substance within the border yet.

319
00:23:31,200 --> 00:23:31,780
So,

320
00:23:33,440 --> 00:23:35,690
this is what you're planning to trade with Chen Meilu?

321
00:23:42,360 --> 00:23:43,620
All these years,

322
00:23:44,790 --> 00:23:46,580
we've had to get our supplies from others

323
00:23:46,960 --> 00:23:48,450
and do whatever they wanted.

324
00:23:51,400 --> 00:23:52,940
It's time we became the suppliers.

325
00:23:57,160 --> 00:23:57,940
From now on,

326
00:23:59,640 --> 00:24:00,820
we'll work together.

327
00:24:05,270 --> 00:24:06,100
We'll split everything fifty-fifty.

328
00:24:07,310 --> 00:24:08,210
What are you doing?

329
00:24:10,230 --> 00:24:11,290
You drink it, I will too.

330
00:24:12,750 --> 00:24:13,660
You said

331
00:24:16,200 --> 00:24:17,900
we'd never touch this stuff ourselves.

332
00:24:21,710 --> 00:24:23,900
I also said I'd never become a supplier.

333
00:24:29,470 --> 00:24:30,730
Times have changed.

334
00:24:42,710 --> 00:24:43,820
What if I refuse?

335
00:24:49,600 --> 00:24:50,730
That's fine.

336
00:24:53,470 --> 00:24:55,050
You're doing pretty well for yourself now.

337
00:24:56,230 --> 00:24:58,450
You can do whatever you want from now on.

338
00:25:00,030 --> 00:25:00,820
No pressure.

339
00:25:35,440 --> 00:25:36,210
That's enough.

340
00:25:42,750 --> 00:25:43,660
As for this stuff,

341
00:25:44,440 --> 00:25:45,340
same rules as always.

342
00:25:45,510 --> 00:25:47,180
Neither of us touches drugs.

343
00:25:48,790 --> 00:25:49,660
We only sell them.

344
00:26:00,400 --> 00:26:01,180
Jiang Ming.

345
00:26:04,550 --> 00:26:06,100
Still testing me?

346
00:26:09,920 --> 00:26:11,530
You're as hotheaded as ever.

347
00:26:11,990 --> 00:26:13,010
You haven't changed a bit.

348
00:26:19,440 --> 00:26:20,250
From now on,

349
00:26:21,400 --> 00:26:22,770
you and I

350
00:26:24,990 --> 00:26:26,380
are going to make a fortune together.

351
00:26:34,400 --> 00:26:35,380
Where will we get our supplies?

352
00:26:37,980 --> 00:26:38,790
[Red Nine-Grid Hot Pot]

353
00:26:38,790 --> 00:26:39,420
Waiter.

354
00:26:39,420 --> 00:26:40,070
[Grand Opening]

355
00:26:40,070 --> 00:26:40,970
Bring us a few beers.

356
00:26:40,990 --> 00:26:41,900
Coming right up.

357
00:26:45,270 --> 00:26:46,420
- It's so crowded. - Waiter, the check.

358
00:26:48,160 --> 00:26:49,450
The more people, the safer we are.

359
00:27:00,470 --> 00:27:01,820
All the raw materials

360
00:27:02,790 --> 00:27:03,420
and equipment

361
00:27:04,360 --> 00:27:05,580
we need are available here.

362
00:27:07,680 --> 00:27:09,450
The factory can produce up to

363
00:27:09,470 --> 00:27:10,820
300 kilograms a day,

364
00:27:11,440 --> 00:27:12,730
operating around the clock.

365
00:27:13,710 --> 00:27:14,820
Once we become the suppliers,

366
00:27:15,920 --> 00:27:17,690
Chen Meilu will handle distribution.

367
00:27:25,030 --> 00:27:26,770
From then on, we'll control the supply.

368
00:27:46,880 --> 00:27:47,690
How does that sound?

369
00:27:55,640 --> 00:27:58,660
Let's sell hot pot together.

370
00:28:01,840 --> 00:28:02,690
Cheers.

371
00:28:08,120 --> 00:28:09,010
The situation is pretty complicated.

372
00:28:16,600 --> 00:28:18,420
This is Director Xu from the Nanhu Anti-Drug Division.

373
00:28:20,790 --> 00:28:21,290
Have a seat.

374
00:28:25,680 --> 00:28:26,820
Captain Yan told me about you.

375
00:28:27,920 --> 00:28:29,730
You played a key role in bringing down Mingkun's organization.

376
00:28:30,310 --> 00:28:32,290
Now you're back undercover.

377
00:28:33,990 --> 00:28:34,860
It hasn't been easy.

378
00:28:39,270 --> 00:28:40,660
Give us an update.

379
00:28:40,960 --> 00:28:42,340
It's safe to talk here.

380
00:28:51,270 --> 00:28:53,860
Bai Ji's factory is in an old air raid shelter.

381
00:28:54,510 --> 00:28:56,530
A hot pot restaurant serves as its cover.

382
00:28:58,160 --> 00:28:59,770
The water and electrical systems are fully equipped.

383
00:28:59,790 --> 00:29:00,900
It's very well concealed.

384
00:29:01,120 --> 00:29:02,380
They've planned everything carefully.

385
00:29:04,510 --> 00:29:06,010
What's the situation inside the factory?

386
00:29:06,920 --> 00:29:08,730
The back of the factory is against a mountainside.

387
00:29:09,310 --> 00:29:11,450
The only way in is through the hot pot restaurant.

388
00:29:11,710 --> 00:29:13,450
There are two gates before you reach the factory.

389
00:29:13,550 --> 00:29:14,490
Both are guarded.

390
00:29:14,960 --> 00:29:16,940
The rooms are reinforced with sheet metal.

391
00:29:17,400 --> 00:29:19,340
The factory is filled with large quantities of

392
00:29:19,360 --> 00:29:20,860
flammable and explosive materials.

393
00:29:23,440 --> 00:29:26,140
They're just as desperate as Mingkun's gang.

394
00:29:26,840 --> 00:29:27,940
If their operation falls apart,

395
00:29:28,880 --> 00:29:30,050
they'll take everyone down with them.

396
00:29:33,750 --> 00:29:35,580
Director Xu has already coordinated with the provincial department.

397
00:29:36,120 --> 00:29:38,340
The SWAT team will also take part in the raid.

398
00:29:39,990 --> 00:29:42,010
Once we've rounded up Bai Ji's entire gang,

399
00:29:42,400 --> 00:29:45,690
you can finally leave undercover work and rejoin us.

400
00:29:48,840 --> 00:29:49,450
All right.

401
00:29:50,230 --> 00:29:51,580
I'll trust you one more time.

402
00:29:52,400 --> 00:29:54,050
Make sure you get every last one of them.

403
00:29:55,160 --> 00:29:56,140
Don't leave anyone behind

404
00:29:56,160 --> 00:29:57,450
to come after me for revenge.

405
00:29:58,920 --> 00:30:00,250
Can't you just quit for good?

406
00:30:00,750 --> 00:30:01,620
Just one last pack.

407
00:30:06,360 --> 00:30:07,860
I'm getting old.

408
00:30:07,880 --> 00:30:09,050
And you're still telling me not to smoke?

409
00:30:10,470 --> 00:30:12,180
When I met you at the police academy at eighteen,

410
00:30:12,200 --> 00:30:13,420
you always had a cigarette in your mouth.

411
00:30:13,920 --> 00:30:15,490
And now you're lecturing me.

412
00:30:16,550 --> 00:30:17,900
You're really getting old.

413
00:30:17,920 --> 00:30:18,730
Look at you.

414
00:30:19,270 --> 00:30:20,530
You're already getting gray hair.

415
00:30:21,310 --> 00:30:22,100
You're thirty already.

416
00:30:22,120 --> 00:30:23,090
How could I not be getting old?

417
00:30:23,880 --> 00:30:25,730
I'm just waiting for you to make a big contribution

418
00:30:25,840 --> 00:30:27,100
so I can retire early.

419
00:30:27,400 --> 00:30:28,580
You want to retire?

420
00:30:29,230 --> 00:30:30,290
You're not even fifty.

421
00:30:30,310 --> 00:30:32,010
You think the department will let you go?

422
00:30:34,470 --> 00:30:35,450
Whether they let me or not

423
00:30:36,960 --> 00:30:37,770
is beside the point.

424
00:30:39,510 --> 00:30:40,290
I can't keep doing this forever.

425
00:30:40,640 --> 00:30:41,450
Fine.

426
00:30:42,400 --> 00:30:43,290
We'll retire together.

427
00:30:43,640 --> 00:30:45,050
Together?

428
00:30:46,510 --> 00:30:47,450
I really don't understand

429
00:30:47,470 --> 00:30:49,180
what goes through you young people's heads.

430
00:30:49,200 --> 00:30:50,100
You want to retire?

431
00:30:50,470 --> 00:30:51,690
All right, let me tell you something.

432
00:30:51,710 --> 00:30:53,210
If I really could retire,

433
00:30:54,510 --> 00:30:55,250
I'd want to find somewhere

434
00:30:55,270 --> 00:30:56,580
nobody knows me

435
00:30:57,510 --> 00:30:58,420
and drive a taxi.

436
00:30:59,840 --> 00:31:02,250
Sounds good. We can team up.

437
00:31:02,960 --> 00:31:04,250
We'll drive taxis during the day

438
00:31:04,270 --> 00:31:06,820
and run a watermelon stand at night.

439
00:31:09,820 --> 00:31:12,770
Then you'll finally get all the watermelon you can eat.

440
00:31:12,790 --> 00:31:13,940
I've always loved watermelon.

441
00:31:23,120 --> 00:31:24,770
Let me tell you the truth.

442
00:31:26,510 --> 00:31:28,250
If you asked me to do something else now,

443
00:31:29,880 --> 00:31:30,940
I wouldn't know how.

444
00:31:34,310 --> 00:31:35,050
I've devoted my whole life

445
00:31:35,710 --> 00:31:37,050
to this work.

446
00:31:37,510 --> 00:31:39,140
I knew you couldn't let it go.

447
00:31:39,400 --> 00:31:40,490
You haven't had enough.

448
00:31:40,710 --> 00:31:42,050
Still hungry for more.

449
00:31:42,640 --> 00:31:43,690
Just enjoying myself.

450
00:31:45,070 --> 00:31:46,900
But there really is something rewarding about it.

451
00:31:47,570 --> 00:31:48,540
Anyone who hasn't done it

452
00:31:48,920 --> 00:31:49,560
wouldn't understand.

453
00:31:56,510 --> 00:31:57,530
We're almost at the finish line.

454
00:32:00,680 --> 00:32:01,620
You must keep your cool.

455
00:32:02,270 --> 00:32:04,290
Your job this time is just to cooperate.

456
00:32:05,710 --> 00:32:06,820
Leave the rest to us.

457
00:32:09,440 --> 00:32:10,210
Don't worry.

458
00:32:12,600 --> 00:32:13,160
I'm off.

459
00:32:18,360 --> 00:32:18,940
Chen Mingsheng.

460
00:32:27,120 --> 00:32:27,900
It's nothing.

461
00:32:53,710 --> 00:32:54,580
Remember this.

462
00:32:56,510 --> 00:32:57,900
As for Jiang Ming's men today,

463
00:32:58,990 --> 00:33:00,100
as long as you don't kill them,

464
00:33:01,310 --> 00:33:02,420
beat them within an inch of their lives.

465
00:33:04,790 --> 00:33:07,140
Boss, shouldn't we think this over?

466
00:33:08,310 --> 00:33:09,450
What's there to think about?

467
00:33:09,470 --> 00:33:10,450
The one thing Mr. Bai hates most

468
00:33:10,470 --> 00:33:11,900
is infighting among our own men.

469
00:33:12,200 --> 00:33:14,140
If we make such a big scene confronting Jiang Ming,

470
00:33:14,470 --> 00:33:16,380
won't we get ourselves into trouble again?

471
00:33:20,230 --> 00:33:21,900
He really knows how to talk.

472
00:33:22,920 --> 00:33:24,050
Get ourselves into trouble?

473
00:33:24,070 --> 00:33:24,970
Again?

474
00:33:26,400 --> 00:33:27,530
Listen up.

475
00:33:28,030 --> 00:33:28,900
As long as he's getting his way,

476
00:33:29,680 --> 00:33:30,770
we'll never get ours.

477
00:33:31,200 --> 00:33:33,010
He pinned the blame on me,

478
00:33:33,310 --> 00:33:34,490
accusing me of swapping the shipment.

479
00:33:34,510 --> 00:33:35,690
And Boss believed him.

480
00:33:36,070 --> 00:33:37,770
Am I supposed to take the blame forever?

481
00:33:39,510 --> 00:33:40,210
So,

482
00:33:40,640 --> 00:33:42,580
I'm going to play to my one strength.

483
00:33:42,600 --> 00:33:43,580
I don't play dirty.

484
00:33:43,960 --> 00:33:44,860
If I'm going after him,

485
00:33:45,440 --> 00:33:46,820
I'll confront him openly.

486
00:33:46,880 --> 00:33:48,450
I'm not putting up with this anymore.

487
00:33:48,550 --> 00:33:49,420
Can you stand it?

488
00:33:49,440 --> 00:33:50,340
No!

489
00:33:50,750 --> 00:33:51,450
Louder!

490
00:33:51,470 --> 00:33:52,900
Can you put up with this?

491
00:33:52,920 --> 00:33:54,050
No!

492
00:33:59,840 --> 00:34:01,490
If we don't settle things with him today,

493
00:34:02,400 --> 00:34:04,530
he'll keep fooling Boss forever.

494
00:34:06,510 --> 00:34:07,290
Little fairy?

495
00:34:21,990 --> 00:34:22,570
Does it hurt?

496
00:34:22,590 --> 00:34:23,010
No.

497
00:34:23,960 --> 00:34:24,570
Does it hurt?

498
00:34:24,590 --> 00:34:25,130
No.

499
00:34:28,470 --> 00:34:29,080
Bai Weiwei.

500
00:34:30,590 --> 00:34:32,090
Don't push your luck just because you've got powerful connections.

501
00:34:35,400 --> 00:34:36,970
You think I wouldn't dare touch you?

502
00:34:43,760 --> 00:34:44,530
Let go of me!

503
00:34:46,030 --> 00:34:47,610
You should thank your brother.

504
00:34:48,150 --> 00:34:49,940
Aren't you afraid this will come back to haunt you?

505
00:34:49,960 --> 00:34:51,300
Keep my brother out of this.

506
00:34:53,400 --> 00:34:55,220
Did you put Jiang Ming in the hospital?

507
00:34:58,590 --> 00:34:59,610
I'm telling you,

508
00:35:01,110 --> 00:35:02,130
Jiang Ming

509
00:35:02,760 --> 00:35:04,050
is one of mine.

510
00:35:04,840 --> 00:35:06,650
Messing with him means messing with me.

511
00:35:07,470 --> 00:35:08,900
If you touch him again,

512
00:35:09,400 --> 00:35:10,380
I'll kill you.

513
00:35:14,190 --> 00:35:15,740
You should read more books.

514
00:35:17,230 --> 00:35:19,900
You're too foolish, Wei.

515
00:35:20,760 --> 00:35:23,090
He's been lying to all of you!

516
00:35:24,960 --> 00:35:26,650
Your whole family

517
00:35:32,190 --> 00:35:33,220
is full of fools!

518
00:35:33,260 --> 00:35:34,550
[Chess and Cards]

519
00:35:34,550 --> 00:35:35,120
Nine of Bamboos.

520
00:35:38,110 --> 00:35:38,640
Kong.

521
00:35:42,550 --> 00:35:43,100
Nine of Bamboos.

522
00:35:47,690 --> 00:35:48,290
Kong.

523
00:35:49,590 --> 00:35:50,070
Mr. Li.

524
00:35:50,560 --> 00:35:51,440
Thanks.

525
00:35:52,360 --> 00:35:52,970
Seven of Bamboos.

526
00:35:57,280 --> 00:35:58,220
Hurry up and play.

527
00:36:00,510 --> 00:36:01,440
I'm done.

528
00:36:01,590 --> 00:36:03,740
I need to go home and cook.

529
00:36:03,760 --> 00:36:04,420
It's getting late.

530
00:36:04,440 --> 00:36:05,530
I need to go home and cook.

531
00:36:05,550 --> 00:36:06,380
Another day.

532
00:36:06,400 --> 00:36:07,130
Another day, another day.

533
00:36:07,150 --> 00:36:08,090
- Okay. - Come play another day.

534
00:36:08,240 --> 00:36:08,740
Come by often.

535
00:36:08,760 --> 00:36:09,460
Yeah, sure.

536
00:36:09,600 --> 00:36:10,860
I was just about to win.

537
00:36:12,440 --> 00:36:12,860
My dear lady,

538
00:36:12,880 --> 00:36:13,860
didn't we agree

539
00:36:13,880 --> 00:36:14,590
you wouldn't come here

540
00:36:14,590 --> 00:36:15,260
to play anymore?

541
00:36:15,590 --> 00:36:17,450
You were going to drive this place out of business.

542
00:36:17,880 --> 00:36:18,450
Why?

543
00:36:18,760 --> 00:36:19,940
I didn't lose last time.

544
00:36:19,960 --> 00:36:20,740
I didn't embarrass us.

545
00:36:20,760 --> 00:36:22,220
That's exactly because you never lose.

546
00:36:22,240 --> 00:36:24,170
They're accusing our place of cheating.

547
00:36:24,360 --> 00:36:25,220
Mahjong!

548
00:36:25,510 --> 00:36:27,860
Full Flush. I win.

549
00:36:27,880 --> 00:36:28,940
Seven Pairs.

550
00:36:29,470 --> 00:36:31,380
Pure Seven Pairs. I win.

551
00:36:32,510 --> 00:36:34,860
Winning on the Last Tile. I win.

552
00:36:35,030 --> 00:36:35,900
Pay up.

553
00:36:40,990 --> 00:36:41,820
Well,

554
00:36:42,510 --> 00:36:43,300
all I can say

555
00:36:44,360 --> 00:36:45,090
is they're terrible players.

556
00:36:45,150 --> 00:36:46,740
The problem is, someone told them

557
00:36:46,760 --> 00:36:48,450
you're Bai Ji's sister.

558
00:36:49,280 --> 00:36:50,610
How am I supposed to explain that?

559
00:36:50,630 --> 00:36:51,970
Even if I gave them this entire place,

560
00:36:51,990 --> 00:36:52,900
it wouldn't be enough to compensate them.

561
00:36:53,630 --> 00:36:54,570
Well, I'm sorry.

562
00:36:55,320 --> 00:36:56,450
Sorry for disrupting your business.

563
00:36:56,470 --> 00:36:57,530
Hope you make a fortune.

564
00:36:57,630 --> 00:36:59,570
No, that's not what I meant.

565
00:36:59,960 --> 00:37:00,530
Where's Jiang Ming?

566
00:37:03,630 --> 00:37:04,940
Ming isn't here.

567
00:37:07,050 --> 00:37:07,570
Really?

568
00:37:07,590 --> 00:37:08,130
Yeah.

569
00:37:10,080 --> 00:37:11,260
- He's not here? - What a shame.

570
00:37:11,590 --> 00:37:12,200
He went out?

571
00:37:14,440 --> 00:37:15,900
He went out? Then I'm leaving.

572
00:37:17,670 --> 00:37:18,490
Weiwei's leaving.

573
00:37:18,990 --> 00:37:20,380
How about some tea before you go?

574
00:37:20,590 --> 00:37:21,220
Get lost.

575
00:37:22,470 --> 00:37:23,610
Stop lying to me.

576
00:37:25,360 --> 00:37:26,130
Jiang Ming.

577
00:37:27,630 --> 00:37:28,490
Jiang Ming.

578
00:37:31,030 --> 00:37:31,420
Well.

579
00:37:31,720 --> 00:37:32,970
You're still alive.

580
00:37:34,030 --> 00:37:35,530
Weiwei, what are you doing here?

581
00:37:36,800 --> 00:37:38,050
You're alive, but you won't answer my calls?

582
00:37:38,720 --> 00:37:39,850
When were you hospitalized?

583
00:37:40,470 --> 00:37:41,940
Was I the last one to find out?

584
00:37:44,280 --> 00:37:45,940
You really do know everything, don't you?

585
00:37:46,880 --> 00:37:48,340
Can you stop joking around?

586
00:37:48,360 --> 00:37:48,780
Seriously, you...

587
00:37:48,800 --> 00:37:49,490
What are you doing?

588
00:37:51,070 --> 00:37:52,090
Let me see where you're hurt.

589
00:37:52,280 --> 00:37:52,940
Don't touch.

590
00:37:53,190 --> 00:37:54,220
Your stomach? Your waist?

591
00:37:54,240 --> 00:37:55,050
No, there's no need.

592
00:37:55,070 --> 00:37:55,450
Let me see.

593
00:37:55,470 --> 00:37:56,050
My back is injured.

594
00:37:56,320 --> 00:37:57,820
You... How are you supposed to see it?

595
00:37:57,840 --> 00:37:59,050
Want me to take my shirt off?

596
00:38:01,510 --> 00:38:02,420
Something's going on with you.

597
00:38:03,840 --> 00:38:04,650
What do you mean?

598
00:38:06,670 --> 00:38:07,740
You've got a woman.

599
00:38:12,440 --> 00:38:13,570
You really do?

600
00:38:14,360 --> 00:38:14,970
What's wrong with that?

601
00:38:18,190 --> 00:38:18,900
If you really have someone,

602
00:38:18,920 --> 00:38:20,530
you have to tell me right away.

603
00:38:20,880 --> 00:38:21,970
I need to make sure she's right for you.

604
00:38:22,760 --> 00:38:25,490
I have a sharp eye. I won't get it wrong.

605
00:38:25,920 --> 00:38:27,130
Let me see where you're hurt.

606
00:38:27,990 --> 00:38:28,700
Don't move.

607
00:38:29,470 --> 00:38:31,130
Looks like the fortune teller was right.

608
00:38:34,110 --> 00:38:35,260
I went to get your fortune told.

609
00:38:35,670 --> 00:38:37,130
They said you'd face a calamity this year.

610
00:38:37,550 --> 00:38:38,970
Looks like it's come true.

611
00:38:39,030 --> 00:38:39,900
May you be safe from now on.

612
00:38:40,440 --> 00:38:40,970
Here.

613
00:38:41,760 --> 00:38:43,090
One for you and one for my brother.

614
00:38:43,590 --> 00:38:45,860
They have both your birth dates and times inside,

615
00:38:46,030 --> 00:38:48,490
along with my blessings for you.

616
00:38:49,960 --> 00:38:51,570
You even know my birth date and time?

617
00:38:51,590 --> 00:38:52,380
Of course.

618
00:38:53,440 --> 00:38:54,970
Mine isn't accurate, though.

619
00:38:55,320 --> 00:38:56,220
Believe it or not.

620
00:38:56,240 --> 00:38:57,050
I believe in it, anyway.

621
00:38:59,190 --> 00:39:00,090
Make sure you keep it safe.

622
00:39:00,720 --> 00:39:02,610
As long as you carry it, you'll be safe.

623
00:39:06,590 --> 00:39:07,380
Thank you.

624
00:39:07,920 --> 00:39:08,700
You're welcome.

625
00:39:16,670 --> 00:39:17,450
Going away?

626
00:39:18,470 --> 00:39:19,170
Yeah.

627
00:39:20,720 --> 00:39:21,970
For a couple of days.

628
00:39:22,670 --> 00:39:24,220
My brother sent you to see Chen Meilu.

629
00:39:26,630 --> 00:39:28,900
Looks like he's putting you in charge of that connection.

630
00:39:30,360 --> 00:39:32,010
You're still so young.

631
00:39:32,030 --> 00:39:33,530
Can't you stop worrying about everything?

632
00:39:34,400 --> 00:39:37,130
What your brother and I do is none of your business.

633
00:39:37,150 --> 00:39:38,780
I'm worried about you.

634
00:39:39,390 --> 00:39:40,940
After that clash with Liu Wei,

635
00:39:40,990 --> 00:39:42,730
and knowing how vindictive he is,

636
00:39:43,120 --> 00:39:44,230
if he doesn't come after you,

637
00:39:44,230 --> 00:39:45,530
he'll go after someone close to you.

638
00:39:45,920 --> 00:39:47,260
You're like a big brother to Wu Jianshan.

639
00:39:47,280 --> 00:39:49,340
You should at least look out for him.

640
00:39:53,100 --> 00:39:55,100
[Langtaosha Chess and Cards]

641
00:39:55,150 --> 00:39:56,010
Ming.

642
00:39:57,320 --> 00:39:58,090
Are you really leaving?

643
00:39:59,440 --> 00:40:00,260
Just for a couple of days.

644
00:40:00,800 --> 00:40:01,780
Keep an eye on things here.

645
00:40:02,550 --> 00:40:03,340
Don't worry.

646
00:40:04,320 --> 00:40:05,300
About Weiwei...

647
00:40:05,630 --> 00:40:06,300
Everything's fine.

648
00:40:08,670 --> 00:40:09,820
What could possibly happen between us?

649
00:40:10,190 --> 00:40:11,820
I... I don't know.

650
00:40:13,190 --> 00:40:14,300
Nothing. It's nothing.

651
00:40:14,670 --> 00:40:16,340
That house caught fire last time.

652
00:40:16,400 --> 00:40:19,010
And there have been a lot of plainclothes officers around.

653
00:40:19,280 --> 00:40:21,260
That woman has moved out, too.

654
00:40:22,550 --> 00:40:23,340
I know.

655
00:40:25,590 --> 00:40:26,970
Look at you, you little rascal.

656
00:40:27,590 --> 00:40:29,010
You've even learned to worry about me now.

657
00:40:29,880 --> 00:40:31,970
When I was thirteen, I helped Mr. Bai deliver a shipment.

658
00:40:31,990 --> 00:40:33,050
I was betrayed on my very first job.

659
00:40:33,280 --> 00:40:34,050
You were the only one who saved me.

660
00:40:34,510 --> 00:40:36,170
What's wrong with showing you some concern?

661
00:40:37,670 --> 00:40:39,050
You be careful, too.

662
00:40:39,440 --> 00:40:40,740
There are police everywhere now.

663
00:40:40,960 --> 00:40:41,570
Don't worry.

664
00:40:42,240 --> 00:40:44,340
If any cop dares set foot in this place,

665
00:40:44,960 --> 00:40:46,530
I'll spot them immediately.

666
00:40:51,070 --> 00:40:51,860
Impressive.

667
00:40:52,760 --> 00:40:53,170
I'm off.

668
00:40:53,760 --> 00:40:54,530
Stay safe, Ming.

669
00:41:11,540 --> 00:41:13,180
♪Forgive me for overthinking...♪

670
00:41:13,800 --> 00:41:14,650
Yes, put it here.

671
00:41:15,620 --> 00:41:18,300
♪What if there's no single answer?♪

672
00:41:21,500 --> 00:41:23,980
♪Sometimes silence, sometimes emptiness♪

673
00:41:24,180 --> 00:41:26,860
♪Sometimes it rains, sometimes all is hazy♪

674
00:41:27,060 --> 00:41:31,620
♪Promises I can barely bring myself to make♪

675
00:41:31,820 --> 00:41:34,100
♪At dusk, the leaves drift down♪

676
00:41:34,380 --> 00:41:36,820
♪Somewhere at the city's edge, pieces of me remain♪

677
00:41:36,980 --> 00:41:39,380
♪So many words I never meant♪

678
00:41:39,580 --> 00:41:41,980
♪I've lost track of all the twists and turns♪

679
00:41:42,220 --> 00:41:46,260
♪Gently kissing the tenderness in your eyes♪

680
00:41:46,780 --> 00:41:49,060
♪Letting it all wash over me♪

681
00:41:51,580 --> 00:41:53,940
♪All the time I've lost to memories♪

682
00:41:54,340 --> 00:41:56,180
♪Hold me close on nights I wake from dreams♪

683
00:41:56,340 --> 00:41:58,860
♪There will always be regrets♪

684
00:41:59,580 --> 00:42:00,380
♪That never shed a tear♪

685
00:42:00,660 --> 00:42:02,100
♪But prove that I was here♪

686
00:42:02,380 --> 00:42:05,060
♪They keep haunting me, leaving me unsteady♪

687
00:42:05,900 --> 00:42:09,340
♪What color will tomorrow be?♪

688
00:42:11,900 --> 00:42:14,140
♪All the time I've lost to memories♪

689
00:42:14,660 --> 00:42:16,420
♪Hold me close on nights I wake from dreams♪

690
00:42:16,660 --> 00:42:19,100
♪There will always be regrets♪

691
00:42:19,780 --> 00:42:20,660
♪That never shed a tear♪

692
00:42:20,860 --> 00:42:22,340
♪But prove that I was here♪

693
00:42:22,620 --> 00:42:25,300
♪They keep haunting me, leaving me unsteady♪

694
00:42:25,940 --> 00:42:29,580
♪What color will tomorrow be?♪

695
00:42:32,660 --> 00:42:35,260
♪What color will it be?♪

696
00:42:53,590 --> 00:42:56,900
The roof leaks a little from time to time.

697
00:42:57,320 --> 00:42:58,490
But it's still perfectly livable.

698
00:42:58,920 --> 00:43:02,170
If you... if you really need to rent somewhere right away,

699
00:43:02,190 --> 00:43:04,260
this is the only room available at the moment.

700
00:43:10,070 --> 00:43:11,650
All right. I'll take it.

701
00:43:13,360 --> 00:43:15,220
It's a little noisy around here.

702
00:43:15,240 --> 00:43:16,380
If noise bothers you,

703
00:43:16,400 --> 00:43:17,740
you'll have to put up with it.

704
00:43:18,110 --> 00:43:19,610
But I can give you a lower rent.

705
00:43:20,550 --> 00:43:23,490
The people upstairs just moved in, too. They're staying short-term.

706
00:43:23,550 --> 00:43:24,970
How long are you planning to stay?

707
00:44:00,420 --> 00:44:02,140
♪I don't say much♪

708
00:44:02,180 --> 00:44:03,900
♪But there's so much going on inside♪

709
00:44:03,980 --> 00:44:07,340
♪I grow more silent as time goes by♪

710
00:44:07,500 --> 00:44:10,460
♪Hard to figure out♪

711
00:44:14,140 --> 00:44:16,020
♪I draw close, then pull away♪

712
00:44:16,060 --> 00:44:17,820
♪It's not that I've never considered it♪

713
00:44:17,900 --> 00:44:21,340
♪I'm just afraid of falling in love again♪

714
00:44:22,100 --> 00:44:26,180
♪And never being able to turn back♪

715
00:44:26,820 --> 00:44:29,220
♪The more rational I try to be, the more I lose control♪

716
00:44:29,260 --> 00:44:31,140
♪The more I hide, the more exposed I feel♪

717
00:44:31,140 --> 00:44:33,820
♪The clearer my mind, the more it hurts♪

718
00:44:34,100 --> 00:44:39,540
♪The more I try to escape, the deeper I fall♪

719
00:44:40,060 --> 00:44:41,220
♪Please♪

720
00:44:41,580 --> 00:44:44,860
♪Don't fall in love with me so easily♪

721
00:44:45,020 --> 00:44:48,460
♪I'm too earnest, too fragile♪

722
00:44:48,580 --> 00:44:51,860
♪I may seem carefree♪

723
00:44:52,060 --> 00:44:55,420
♪But I'm hurting more than anyone♪

724
00:44:55,620 --> 00:44:58,820
♪Don't see right through me so easily♪

725
00:44:59,060 --> 00:45:02,140
♪Afraid of crowds, afraid of loneliness♪

726
00:45:02,300 --> 00:45:07,140
♪Afraid I'll fall hopelessly in love with you♪

727
00:45:10,420 --> 00:45:13,380
♪A tenderness I was born with♪

728
00:45:13,540 --> 00:45:16,140
♪So easily traps me♪

729
00:45:17,500 --> 00:45:20,020
♪A greeting offered out of courtesy♪

730
00:45:20,340 --> 00:45:23,820
♪Captures me in a second♪

731
00:45:24,300 --> 00:45:26,980
♪Standing at a crossroads♪

732
00:45:27,460 --> 00:45:30,820
♪I don't know what to do♪

733
00:45:30,900 --> 00:45:32,380
♪My heart♪

734
00:45:32,660 --> 00:45:36,140
♪Floats in midair♪

735
00:45:36,940 --> 00:45:37,660
♪So♪

736
00:45:37,900 --> 00:45:41,020
♪Don't fall in love with me so easily♪

737
